{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"WAVE 1 - METHOD. 10 rebar tickets, each contributing a BLOCK-state plan and its later PASS-state plan, giving a within-ticket control. Ticket state is reconstructed with 'git archive <tickets_sha> <dir> | tar -x' into a PLAIN directory - never a git worktree, because REBAR_TRACKER_DIR on a worktree makes rebar run store maintenance and delete history. Six metrics per METHODOLOGY.md: TP requires accurate AND material; an FP requires opening the cited file at the pinned SHA and quoting the disproving excerpt (never asserted from reasoning); nits are accurate-but-immaterial; UNVERIFIABLE is its own bucket. Judging is delegated to independent subagents under a binding contract in harness/JUDGE_INSTRUCTIONS.md; the orchestrator does not score."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789000635525949001,"uuid":"58459e8a-e1f2-4131-8434-851ff9285a31"}